From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:20:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] northbridge/intel/haswell: Name the DIMMs by their slot in
 SMBIOS

setup_sdram_meminfo() takes the size and ranks of slot N from field N
of MAD_DIMM, but the two fields are DIMM A and DIMM B, and bit 16 (DIMM
A select) says which slot DIMM A is. The native RAM init makes the
larger DIMM DIMM A (configure_mc.c, .dimm_a_sel = biggest), and on an
mrc.bin build the bit is whatever mrc.bin programs. With the larger DIMM
in slot 1, SMBIOS type 17 then gives slot 0 the size and ranks of slot
1 with the part number and serial of slot 0, and slot 1 the other size;
dmidecode and hw-report name the wrong module. The next commit makes
this certain in the case it is about: when it leaves out the DIMM of
slot 0, slot 1 becomes DIMM A, and SMBIOS would list the module left
out with the size of the one in use.

Take for each slot the field that bit 16 maps to it, for the size and
the ranks; the SPD strings already come from the slot. With bit 16
clear the fields map as before: equal DIMMs, as the four 8 GiB
SO-DIMMs of the W541, keep the same records. The code is shared by
mrc.bin and the native RAM init and by the W541 and the T440p, and the
fix is meant for all of them.

TEST=Host syntax check with -Werror and the ci-150 W541 nri and mrc
configs. Host unit test of setup_sdram_meminfo() with MCHBAR mapped at
its fixed address and synthetic SPD strings: channel 0 with slot 0
empty and slot 1 DIMM A (8 GiB, dual rank) gives one record, slot 1,
with its own part number and serial; channel 1 with 4 GiB single rank
in slot 0 and 8 GiB dual rank in slot 1 gives each slot its size and
ranks; four equal DIMMs with bit 16 clear give the same records as
before. The code before this change fails 6 of these checks. Still to
test on the W541 (both variants): dmidecode -t 17 unchanged with the
four 8 GiB DIMMs; with DIMMs of two sizes in a channel, if at hand, each
slot shows its own module.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/raminit_shared.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/raminit_shared.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/raminit_shared.c
index 608e0b343f..e8e0b68eea 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/raminit_shared.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/raminit_shared.c
@@ -159,15 +159,19 @@ void setup_sdram_meminfo(const uint8_t *spd_data[NUM_CHANNELS][NUM_SLOTS])
 	unsigned int dimm_cnt = 0;
 	for (unsigned int channel = 0; channel < NUM_CHANNELS; channel++) {
 		const uint32_t ch_conf = mchbar_read32(MAD_DIMM(channel));
+		/* Bit 16 selects the slot of DIMM A (the larger one), DIMM B is the other */
+		const unsigned int dimm_a_slot = (ch_conf >> 16) & 1;
 		for (unsigned int slot = 0; slot < NUM_SLOTS; slot++) {
-			const uint32_t dimm_size = ((ch_conf >> (slot * 8)) & 0xff) * 256;
+			/* The MAD_DIMM fields of this slot: 0 for DIMM A, 1 for DIMM B */
+			const unsigned int field = slot != dimm_a_slot;
+			const uint32_t dimm_size = ((ch_conf >> (field * 8)) & 0xff) * 256;
 			if (dimm_size) {
 				struct dimm_info *dimm = &mem_info->dimm[dimm_cnt];
 				dimm->dimm_size = dimm_size;
 				/* TODO: Hardcoded, could also be LPDDR3 */
 				dimm->ddr_type = MEMORY_TYPE_DDR3;
 				dimm->ddr_frequency = ddr_freq_mhz * 2; /* In MT/s */
-				dimm->rank_per_dimm = 1 + ((ch_conf >> (17 + slot)) & 1);
+				dimm->rank_per_dimm = 1 + ((ch_conf >> (17 + field)) & 1);
 				dimm->channel_num = channel;
 				dimm->dimm_num = slot;
 				dimm->bank_locator = channel * 2;
-- 
